window.DE_CHUNKS=window.DE_CHUNKS||[];window.DE_CHUNKS.push([{"id":487,"unit":5,"q":"In a half-subtractor circuit with X and Y as inputs, the Borrow (M) and Difference (N = X - Y) are given by M=X'Y,N=X⨁Y 1 M=X ⨁Y,N=XY M=XY,N=X⨁Y M=X'Y,N=X⨁Y M=X'Y,N=(X⨁Y)'","k":"","s":["Half-subtractor: Difference=A⊕B, Borrow=A'B.","Truth table (A,B → D,Borrow): 00→00, 01→11, 10→10, 11→00."]},{"id":488,"unit":5,"q":"A combinational logic circuit has memory characteristics that \"remember\" the inputs after they have been removed.","k":"False","s":["Correct option: False.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":489,"unit":5,"q":"To implement the full-adder sum functions, two exclusive-OR gates can be used.True","k":"","s":["Write the required truth table or Boolean expression.","Simplify it with Boolean algebra or a K-map where appropriate.","Draw the labelled gate-level circuit from the simplified equation."]},{"id":490,"unit":5,"q":"A half-adder does not have ________.","k":"A","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]},{"id":491,"unit":5,"q":"Which of the statements below best describes the given figure?","k":"A","s":["Correct option: A.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":492,"unit":5,"q":"A full-adder adds ________.","k":"A","s":["Correct option: A.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":493,"unit":5,"q":"The carry propagation delay in 4-bit full-adder circuits:","k":"A","s":["Correct option: A.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":494,"unit":5,"q":"Two 4-bit binary numbers (1011 and 1111) are applied to a 4-bit parallel adder. The carry input is 1. What are the values for the sum and carry output?C 1 ∑4 ∑3 ∑2 ∑1=0111, Cout = 0 ∑4 ∑3 ∑2 ∑1 = 1111, Cout = 1 ∑4 ∑3 ∑2 ∑1= 1011, Cout = 1 ∑4 ∑3 ∑2 ∑1= 1100, Cout =","k":"","s":["Identify the required Boolean relation or circuit from the question.","Apply the relevant truth table, Boolean theorem, K-map or combinational-circuit equation.","Write the simplified final result and include the requested logic diagram when needed."]},{"id":495,"unit":5,"q":"A full-adder has a Cin = 0. What are the sum and the carry (Cout) when A = 1 and B = 1?","k":"B","s":["Correct option: B.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":496,"unit":5,"q":"An adder in which bits of the operand are added one after another__________C 1 Half adder Half subtractor Serial Adder parallel Adder","k":"","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]},{"id":497,"unit":5,"q":"What is the major difference between half-adders and full-adders?","k":"C","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]},{"id":498,"unit":5,"q":"A combinational circuit calculates the arithmetic sum in a parallel way. What is the name of the adder?","k":"B","s":["Correct option: B.","This matches the answer key in the supplied practice book."]},{"id":499,"unit":5,"q":"To implement a half adder and half subtractor ,the no. of basic(AND,OR,NOT) gates required is____ and ____ respectively. 6,5","k":"","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]},{"id":500,"unit":5,"q":"A binary half-subtractor having two inputs A and B, the correct set of logical outputs D(=A minus B) and X(=borrow) are 1.The difference output D=A'B+AB' 2.The borrow output B=AB' Which of the above is/are correct?","k":"A","s":["Half-subtractor: Difference=A⊕B, Borrow=A'B.","Truth table (A,B → D,Borrow): 00→00, 01→11, 10→10, 11→00."]},{"id":501,"unit":5,"q":"The number of full and half-adders required to add 16-bit numbers is","k":"B","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]},{"id":502,"unit":5,"q":"How Serial Adder differ from Parallel Adders? a serial adder processes bits one pair at a time sequentially over multiple clock cycles, while a parallel adder processes all bits simultaneously in a single clock cycle.","k":"","s":["Serial adder uses one full adder repeatedly, one bit pair per clock: less hardware but slower.","Parallel adder uses one adder stage per bit so all bit positions work together: faster but more hardware."]},{"id":503,"unit":5,"q":"The half-adder can be implemented from which of the following equation?D 1 S = xy′ + x′y C = xy S = (x + y) (x′ + y′) C = x y S = (C + x′y′)′ C = xy All of above","k":"","s":["Half-adder: Sum=A⊕B, Carry=AB.","Truth table (A,B → S,C): 00→00, 01→10, 10→10, 11→01."]}]);